            <div xml:id="d86">

                <pb facs="0181" n="79" sameAs="frus:frus1935v01/pg79"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">500.A15A5/440a: Telegram</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Acting Secretary of State to the Ambassador in
                        Japan</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic">Grew</hi>)</head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Washington</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1935-07-13T16:00:00-04:00">July 13, 1935—4
                            p.m.</date>
                    </dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>106. Our Embassy at Berlin was told in strict confidence by the German Ministry
                    of Marine that Japan objects to German participation in the next Naval
                    Conference on the pretext that this would increase the representation of the
                    white races as against the yellow. Have you any confirmatory information?</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Phillips</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
